    {
      "id": "block.code.backtick-in-info-is-inline-code",
      "spec": "2.4",
      "source": "` ```math ` opens an inline code span at line start\n",
      "expect": {
        "normal": { "valid": true, "canonical": "```` ```math ```` opens an inline code span at line start\n" },
        "strict": {
          "valid": false,
          "diagnostics": [{ "category": "noncanonical", "severity": "error" }]
        }
      },
      "semanticAst": {
        "type": "document",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              { "type": "inlineCode", "value": "```math " },
              { "type": "text", "value": " opens an inline code span at line start" }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "footnotes": []
      },
      "notes": "A `` ```+ `` line whose remainder contains a backtick is not a code fence (the info token may not contain a backtick, §2.4); it is a paragraph whose leading run opens an inline code span, matching CommonMark. The canonical surface widens the delimiter to four backticks."
    },
    {
      "id": "block.code.backtick-fence-info-token",
      "spec": "2.4",
      "source": "````math ``` ```` is inline code, not a fence\n",
      "expect": {
        "normal": { "valid": true, "canonical": "````math ``` ```` is inline code, not a fence\n" },
        "strict": { "valid": true, "canonical": "````math ``` ```` is inline code, not a fence\n" }
      },
      "semanticAst": {
        "type": "document",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              { "type": "inlineCode", "value": "math ```" },
              { "type": "text", "value": " is inline code, not a fence" }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "footnotes": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "block.code.backtick-in-info-does-not-interrupt-paragraph",
      "spec": "2.4",
      "source": "A paragraph line.\n```` ```math ```` still the same paragraph\n",
      "expect": {
        "normal": { "valid": true, "canonical": "A paragraph line.\n```` ```math ```` still the same paragraph\n" },
        "strict": { "valid": true, "canonical": "A paragraph line.\n```` ```math ```` still the same paragraph\n" }
      },
      "semanticAst": {
        "type": "document",
        "children": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "children": [
              { "type": "text", "value": "A paragraph line." },
              { "type": "softBreak" },
              { "type": "inlineCode", "value": "```math " },
              { "type": "text", "value": " still the same paragraph" }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "footnotes": []
      },
      "notes": "A `` ```+ `` line whose remainder holds a backtick is not a fence (§2.4), so it does not interrupt an in-progress paragraph — it is a continuation line whose leading run opens an inline code span. Exercises the `startsFence` recogniser."
    },
